    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What is Rayuela?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It is a competition where you throw a coin-like object (Tejo) to a box, and whoever gets closer to the line in the box is the winner, but what if we has a twist in this game?... what if the Tejos and Boxes were made of different materials?... well, this is &quot;A Rayuela Game!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Your main objective is to participate in the 9 available tournaments and defeat the opponents in those tournaments to become the world champion.</strong> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3744360/extras/2449e0c54bacd5529aec44ebf39c51f1.avif?t=1748762188\" data-has-big width=800 height=454 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You must throw the Tejos as close as possible to the line drawn inside the Box.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But it won\u2019t be easy\u2014the first Tejos you can acquire are made of cheap materials, which will make winning certain tournaments more difficult. However, each Rayuela match grants you &quot;coins&quot; (the in-game currency), which you can use to buy more Tejos made from different materials. This allows you to choose the best option depending on the type of box used in each tournament.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>But... What is Rayuela? What are Tejos? And what are Boxes?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rayuela</strong> is the match you play against your opponent\u2014both players take turns throwing a circular object (Tejo), which must land as close as possible to the line drawn inside the box. The player whose Tejo lands closest to the line wins the match.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In a standard Rayuela match, several turns are played. However, in &quot;A Rayuela Game,&quot; you only have one chance\u2014you either win or lose.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tejos</strong> are the circular objects used to be thrown onto the surface of a Box, which has a line drawn in the middle.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Boxes</strong> are simply... boxes! They are the surfaces where the Tejo must land to determine which player is the winner.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3744360/extras/78f10ce0abf8226b789ac09665bea77e.avif?t=1748762188\" data-has-big width=800 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>How many Tejos and Boxes are available?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can acquire up to 12 Tejos and 9 Boxes, each with a behavior similar to the material it is named after.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tejos:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Paper </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Rubber </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Wood </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Bone </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Cardbox </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Clay </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Fabric </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Glass </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Hard Plastic </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Leaves </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Meat </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Metal </i></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Boxes:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Clay </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Fabric</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Glass </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Leaves</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Metal </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Plastic </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Rubber </i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Stone</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Wood</i></p></li></ul>",
